  "answer_text": "The original **Spiegel catalog** (and its online store, `spiegel.com`) is **permanently out of business**. \n\nIf you have been searching for the Spiegel home catalog to shop online, the following details explain what happened to the company and point you toward alternatives for home and fashion catalog shopping.\n\n---\n\n### What Happened to Spiegel?\n* **A Long History:** Founded in 1865 by Joseph Spiegel as a furniture store in Chicago, Spiegel launched its iconic mail-order catalogs in 1905. For over a century, it was a household staple, famed for introducing American consumers to European fashion trends, high-quality home goods, and revolutionary installment payment plans.\n* **The Digital Shift:** Facing severe financial struggles in the early 2000s, the company declared bankruptcy in 2003. After being purchased by Patriarch Partners, the company discontinued its famous thick paper catalogs in favor of a digital-only storefront at `spiegel.com`, focusing primarily on women's fashion and lifestyle products.\n* **The Sudden Shutdown:** Between late 2019 and early 2020, Spiegel quietly and abruptly shut down. The website was taken offline without warning, bringing an end to the brand's historic run.\n\n---\n\n### Where to Find Vintage Spiegel Catalogs & Items\nIf you are looking for Spiegel for nostalgic reasons or want to collect vintage items, you can still find them online:\n* **Vintage Catalogs & Goods:** You can regularly find physical vintage Spiegel catalogs (dating from the mid-20th century to the early 2000s), vintage apparel, and home decor items on **[eBay](https://www.ebay.com)** or **[Etsy](https://www.etsy.com)**.\n* **Digital Archives:** If you just want to browse old Spiegel catalogs for mid-century modern design inspiration, many editions have been digitized and can be read for free on the **[Internet Archive](https://archive.org)**.\n\n---\n\n### Alternative Online Home Shopping Catalogs\nIf you loved the style, convenience, and catalog-format of Spiegel for home goods and decor, several active online retailers offer a similar shopping experience:\n\n1. **[BrylaneHome](https://www.brylanehome.com):** Excellent for colorful bedding, bath accessories, kitchen electrics, and outdoor furniture. They still offer a physical mail-order catalog alongside their online store.\n2. **[Country Door](https://www.countrydoor.com):** A great option if you prefer a cozy, rustic, or modern farmhouse aesthetic. They offer easy-to-browse digital catalogs and home decor.\n3. **[The Lakeside Collection](https://www.lakeside.com):** Known for highly affordable home decor, unique kitchen gadgets, organizing solutions, and seasonal holiday decorations. \n4. **[Montgomery Ward](https://www.wards.com):** Originally one of Spiegel's primary catalog rivals. While the historic department store is gone, Montgomery Ward lives on as an active online-and-catalog retailer offering home furnishings, electronics, and apparel.",
